[{:db/id "q-331026/selection/b258b8a477003d5fac8673ca549a6f966209c9a7b671adcfaa5ca049b17a091c" :answer/id #uuid "78f9e325-e7a5-5ae0-9f56-efa11abeecac" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{e}^{-14s}(\\frac{2}{{s}^{3}}+\\frac{23}{{s}^{2}})" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-331026/selection/9b3fcb1d7deafd4c31ef30d3e4f3b01146e52ae2a6a4da98df50d31bfdb163c8" :answer/id #uuid "92db6f5f-57a2-5438-9d0f-b00cdebc86fd" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{e}^{-14s}(\\frac{1}{{s}^{3}}+\\frac{-5}{{s}^{2}}+\\frac{4}{s})" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-331026/selection/00fe0b92c90ac9cc84dc9268d79bdc2e4755f5b20571a0a25fd3a1fe3845768f" :answer/id #uuid "ed7df329-055e-58eb-867e-d0c24542222f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{e}^{14s}(\\frac{2}{{s}^{3}}-\\frac{23}{{s}^{2}})" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-331026/selection/0b9e2b9ad959ffff0fb58be8516781bdea8f6e71677d89c09fe3dad8cf20f6c2" :answer/id #uuid "c3f5d077-34b8-5c17-bf9f-a9ed3b4fe878" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{e}^{-14s}(\\frac{2}{{s}^{3}}+\\frac{23}{{s}^{2}}+\\frac{130}{s})" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-331026/selection/f52845111cdad0cd06f3a05133642c0d2e93abeebef921d148806e36e8651baf" :answer/id #uuid "39dc2c0d-1f92-5dfa-a0c1-25b17f08a645" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{e}^{-s}(\\frac{2}{{s}^{3}}+\\frac{23}{{s}^{2}}+\\frac{130}{s})" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-331026/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "1cd77848-4a31-5628-bd38-832dc44172c5" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-331026/selection/0b9e2b9ad959ffff0fb58be8516781bdea8f6e71677d89c09fe3dad8cf20f6c2" :answer-field/choices ["q-331026/selection/b258b8a477003d5fac8673ca549a6f966209c9a7b671adcfaa5ca049b17a091c" "q-331026/selection/9b3fcb1d7deafd4c31ef30d3e4f3b01146e52ae2a6a4da98df50d31bfdb163c8" "q-331026/selection/00fe0b92c90ac9cc84dc9268d79bdc2e4755f5b20571a0a25fd3a1fe3845768f" "q-331026/selection/0b9e2b9ad959ffff0fb58be8516781bdea8f6e71677d89c09fe3dad8cf20f6c2" "q-331026/selection/f52845111cdad0cd06f3a05133642c0d2e93abeebef921d148806e36e8651baf"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-331026" :question/id #uuid "4b7dd261-0c69-5613-9ae3-ff2b1fcb4deb" :question/math-academy-id "q-331026" :question/problem "Given that $L{{t}^{n}}=\\frac{n!}{{s}^{n+1}}$ for $s>0$, find $L{u(t-14)({t}^{2}-5t+4)},$ where $u(t)$ is the unit step function." :question/worked-solution "The second shifting theorem states that if $a\\ge 0$ and $L{u(t-a)\\,g(t)}$ exists for $s>{s}_{0},$ then\n\n$$\nL{u(t-a)\\,g(t)}={e}^{-as}\\,L{g(t+a)},\\,\\text{for}\\,s>{s}_{0},\n$$\n\nwhere $u(t)$ is the unit step function.\n\nIn our case, we wish to find\n\n$$\nL{u(t-14)({t}^{2}-5t+4)}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, $a=14,$ and we have \n\n$$\nL{u(t-14)\\,g(t)}={e}^{-14s}\\,L{g(t+14)},\n$$\n\nwhere $g(t)={t}^{2}-5t+4.$\n\nNotice that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}g(t+14) & =(t+14)^{2}-5(t+14)+4 \\\\  & ={t}^{2}+28t+196\\,-\\,5t-70\\,+\\,4 \\\\  & ={t}^{2}+23t+130.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $L{{t}^{n}}=\\frac{n!}{{s}^{n+1}}$ and $L{1}=\\frac{1}{s}$ for $s>0,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L{g(t+14)} & =L{{t}^{2}+23t+130} \\\\  & =L{{t}^{2}}+23L{t}+130L{1} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{{s}^{3}}+23\\cdot \\frac{1}{{s}^{2}}+130\\cdot \\frac{1}{s} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{{s}^{3}}+\\frac{23}{{s}^{2}}+\\frac{130}{s}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, applying the second shifting theorem, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L{u(t-14)\\,g(t)} & ={e}^{-14s}\\,L{g(t+14)} \\\\  & ={e}^{-14s}(\\frac{2}{{s}^{3}}+\\frac{23}{{s}^{2}}+\\frac{130}{s}).\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-331026/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "7a93711c-90bc-52d2-905f-80b2c1fc487b"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-331026"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-331016"] :question/problem "Given that $L{{t}^{n}}=\\frac{n!}{{s}^{n+1}}$ for $s>0$, find $L{u(t-5)({t}^{2}+4t+1)},$ where $u(t)$ is the unit step function." :question/worked-solution "The second shifting theorem states that if $a\\ge 0$ and $L{u(t-a)\\,g(t)}$ exists for $s>{s}_{0},$ then\n\n$$\nL{u(t-a)\\,g(t)}={e}^{-as}\\,L{g(t+a)},\\,\\text{for}\\,s>{s}_{0},\n$$\n\nwhere $u(t)$ is the unit step function.\n\nIn our case, we wish to find\n\n$$\nL{u(t-5)({t}^{2}+4t+1)}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, $a=5,$ and we have \n\n$$\nL{u(t-5)\\,g(t)}={e}^{-5s}\\,L{g(t+5)},\n$$\n\nwhere $g(t)={t}^{2}+4t+1.$\n\nNotice that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}g(t+5) & =(t+5)^{2}+4(t+5)+1 \\\\  & ={t}^{2}+10t+25\\,+\\,4t+20\\,+\\,1 \\\\  & ={t}^{2}+14t+46.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $L{{t}^{n}}=\\frac{n!}{{s}^{n+1}}$ and $L{1}=\\frac{1}{s}$ for $s>0,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L{g(t+5)} & =L{{t}^{2}+14t+46} \\\\  & =L{{t}^{2}}+14L{t}+46L{1} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{{s}^{3}}+14\\cdot \\frac{1}{{s}^{2}}+46\\cdot \\frac{1}{s} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{{s}^{3}}+\\frac{14}{{s}^{2}}+\\frac{46}{s}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, applying the second shifting theorem, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L{u(t-5)\\,g(t)} & ={e}^{-5s}\\,L{g(t+5)} \\\\  & ={e}^{-5s}(\\frac{2}{{s}^{3}}+\\frac{14}{{s}^{2}}+\\frac{46}{s}).\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-331017/selection/d982ae9182d333aab71892cfa49abec5902901e71bc8cdf64f7ba73ae48d69d8" :answer/id #uuid "c7f4c672-5cb1-5208-b806-216782bb9953" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{e}^{-s}(\\frac{2}{{s}^{3}}+\\frac{11}{{s}^{2}}+\\frac{33}{s})" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-331017/selection/3ef0ae3ab3ded2c7f7dbb057ef4f2b68296cddb1ba145b6d9eb87a25af31dc8f" :answer/id #uuid "7d7f516a-0e0d-538c-b911-ac0b69a8f25a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{e}^{6s}(\\frac{2}{{s}^{3}}-\\frac{11}{{s}^{2}})" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-331017/selection/2c050357dab17fd32b48336e5dfab10038e867c2e81f734ddd2668439c051d3f" :answer/id #uu