(t)$ is the unit step function.\n\nIn our case, we wish to find\n\n$$\nL{u(t-6)({t}^{2}-t+3)}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, $a=6,$ and we have \n\n$$\nL{u(t-6)\\,g(t)}={e}^{-6s}\\,L{g(t+6)},\n$$\n\nwhere $g(t)={t}^{2}-t+3.$\n\nNotice that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}g(t+6) & =(t+6)^{2}-(t+6)+3 \\\\  & ={t}^{2}+12t+36\\,-\\,t-6\\,+\\,3 \\\\  & ={t}^{2}+11t+33.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $L{{t}^{n}}=\\frac{n!}{{s}^{n+1}}$ and $L{1}=\\frac{1}{s}$ for $s>0,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L{g(t+6)} & =L{{t}^{2}+11t+33} \\\\  & =L{{t}^{2}}+11L{t}+33L{1} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{{s}^{3}}+11\\cdot \\frac{1}{{s}^{2}}+33\\cdot \\frac{1}{s} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{{s}^{3}}+\\frac{11}{{s}^{2}}+\\frac{33}{s}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, applying the second shifting theorem, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L{u(t-6)\\,g(t)} & ={e}^{-6s}\\,L{g(t+6)} \\\\  & ={e}^{-6s}(\\frac{2}{{s}^{3}}+\\frac{11}{{s}^{2}}+\\frac{33}{s}).\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-331017/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "7a93711c-90bc-52d2-905f-80b2c1fc487b"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-331017"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-331025/selection/6d6275114cacce4454db95a65132fd6fc323c2275801f6d9d5cbecf650805843" :answer/id #uuid "b05ca2a1-0de2-5f98-9699-154373df0b1a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{e}^{-s}(\\frac{2}{{s}^{3}}+\\frac{20}{{s}^{2}}+\\frac{104}{s})" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-331025/selection/53b9b3020ca911a65c8d288acdce63431cee27bcda04a9171c7bb8e9381f149f" :answer/id #uuid "a812825c-4b91-5372-9eca-b13df4980fce" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{e}^{-11s}(\\frac{2}{{s}^{3}}+\\frac{20}{{s}^{2}})" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-331025/selection/4a78a5c679caf78a56fca17ccac632821da062900d5d79dad57eff0d26228b5f" :answer/id #uuid "3f4113db-3e81-5c2f-9df3-1f15e57ae188" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{e}^{-11s}(\\frac{2}{{s}^{3}}+\\frac{20}{{s}^{2}}+\\frac{104}{s})" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-331025/selection/1b25635d9e9a2c6df4072367e50e4c338295e2c01600d8e74270c2b9cb83b83d" :answer/id #uuid "9411e455-ab33-5f79-94d1-e7364e5c522d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{e}^{-11s}(\\frac{1}{{s}^{3}}+\\frac{-2}{{s}^{2}}+\\frac{5}{s})" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-331025/selection/f551ed2b87b3e75a93a12c1511bab7ffe83dfedfd439f6f2bdc3b26f0e2af260" :answer/id #uuid "bc35f188-d5c1-5f4c-b479-8af8312c8b92" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{e}^{11s}(\\frac{2}{{s}^{3}}-\\frac{20}{{s}^{2}})" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-331025/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "c2bf4089-2131-5330-943d-2eccfa4f85a1" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-331025/selection/4a78a5c679caf78a56fca17ccac632821da062900d5d79dad57eff0d26228b5f" :answer-field/choices ["q-331025/selection/6d6275114cacce4454db95a65132fd6fc323c2275801f6d9d5cbecf650805843" "q-331025/selection/53b9b3020ca911a65c8d288acdce63431cee27bcda04a9171c7bb8e9381f149f" "q-331025/selection/4a78a5c679caf78a56fca17ccac632821da062900d5d79dad57eff0d26228b5f" "q-331025/selection/1b25635d9e9a2c6df4072367e50e4c338295e2c01600d8e74270c2b9cb83b83d" "q-331025/selection/f551ed2b87b3e75a93a12c1511bab7ffe83dfedfd439f6f2bdc3b26f0e2af260"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-331025" :question/id #uuid "d50b6b30-ecc6-55ea-9bc0-857c1dec78ee" :question/math-academy-id "q-331025" :question/problem "Given that $L{{t}^{n}}=\\frac{n!}{{s}^{n+1}}$ for $s>0$, find $L{u(t-11)({t}^{2}-2t+5)},$ where $u(t)$ is the unit step function." :question/worked-solution "The second shifting theorem states that if $a\\ge 0$ and $L{u(t-a)\\,g(t)}$ exists for $s>{s}_{0},$ then\n\n$$\nL{u(t-a)\\,g(t)}={e}^{-as}\\,L{g(t+a)},\\,\\text{for}\\,s>{s}_{0},\n$$\n\nwhere $u(t)$ is the unit step function.\n\nIn our case, we wish to find\n\n$$\nL{u(t-11)({t}^{2}-2t+5)}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, $a=11,$ and we have \n\n$$\nL{u(t-11)\\,g(t)}={e}^{-11s}\\,L{g(t+11)},\n$$\n\nwhere $g(t)={t}^{2}-2t+5.$\n\nNotice that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}g(t+11) & =(t+11)^{2}-2(t+11)+5 \\\\  & ={t}^{2}+22t+121\\,-\\,2t-22\\,+\\,5 \\\\  & ={t}^{2}+20t+104.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $L{{t}^{n}}=\\frac{n!}{{s}^{n+1}}$ and $L{1}=\\frac{1}{s}$ for $s>0,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L{g(t+11)} & =L{{t}^{2}+20t+104} \\\\  & =L{{t}^{2}}+20L{t}+104L{1} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{{s}^{3}}+20\\cdot \\frac{1}{{s}^{2}}+104\\cdot \\frac{1}{s} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{{s}^{3}}+\\frac{20}{{s}^{2}}+\\frac{104}{s}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, applying the second shifting theorem, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L{u(t-11)\\,g(t)} & ={e}^{-11s}\\,L{g(t+11)} \\\\  & ={e}^{-11s}(\\frac{2}{{s}^{3}}+\\frac{20}{{s}^{2}}+\\frac{104}{s}).\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-331025/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "7a93711c-90bc-52d2-905f-80b2c1fc487b"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-331025"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-331019/selection/2c3600882244fe38b38f4df4f6c53ae67c795e252479382c8d6065439ca084f8" :answer/id #uuid "45783918-e074-5533-a3dc-ea33abef94e2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{e}^{-8s}(\\frac{1}{{s}^{3}}+\\frac{5}{{s}^{2}}+\\frac{-1}{s})" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-331019/selection/e0647253fc78adba4769a96ca7f06076d90b522015b0ac0b4a818b91997d57ed" :answer/id #uuid "b34e78b8-b5d5-50af-9443-45d1770fe403" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{e}^{-8s}(\\frac{2}{{s}^{3}}+\\frac{21}{{s}^{2}})" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-331019/selection/af33d81bb015c448e4b2b72ed86fafff841eaa577df4bbe00a14710fd813aded" :answer/id #uuid "ca0ba15b-670c-5df9-9bfa-c1b37461477f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{e}^{-8s}(\\frac{2}{{s}^{3}}+\\frac{21}{{s}^{2}}+\\frac{103}{s})" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-331019/selection/bd666f6