Notice that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}g(t+8) & =(t+8)^{2}+5(t+8)-1 \\\\  & ={t}^{2}+16t+64\\,+\\,5t+40\\,-\\,1 \\\\  & ={t}^{2}+21t+103.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $L{{t}^{n}}=\\frac{n!}{{s}^{n+1}}$ and $L{1}=\\frac{1}{s}$ for $s>0,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L{g(t+8)} & =L{{t}^{2}+21t+103} \\\\  & =L{{t}^{2}}+21L{t}+103L{1} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{{s}^{3}}+21\\cdot \\frac{1}{{s}^{2}}+103\\cdot \\frac{1}{s} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{{s}^{3}}+\\frac{21}{{s}^{2}}+\\frac{103}{s}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, applying the second shifting theorem, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L{u(t-8)\\,g(t)} & ={e}^{-8s}\\,L{g(t+8)} \\\\  & ={e}^{-8s}(\\frac{2}{{s}^{3}}+\\frac{21}{{s}^{2}}+\\frac{103}{s}).\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-331019/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "7a93711c-90bc-52d2-905f-80b2c1fc487b"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-331019"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-331039/selection/dd1a4a3c7090169e73093aecca884576b55cf87dd14dafd5a8c4b8bc93b4f414" :answer/id #uuid "6bd8be68-0e59-58a7-b46b-7aa856286023" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-{e}^{-s}\\cdot \\frac{s}{{s}^{2}+25{\\pi }^{2}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-331039/selection/6fa0ebd5d3d267d83a4af36945026e0eec615ab545d18b185ff4acab4ba2aaf8" :answer/id #uuid "c6e66e90-a953-59cc-a9ba-d796578167a0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{e}^{-s}\\cdot \\frac{s}{{s}^{2}+25{\\pi }^{2}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-331039/selection/61b0be8399d0736c70c106a293a36dfcdeec4f3603994c83f678deb760e9db2d" :answer/id #uuid "fbe42840-be96-53a7-b91a-f72d9b222d6c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-{e}^{-5s}\\cdot \\frac{5\\pi }{{s}^{2}+25{\\pi }^{2}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-331039/selection/ad60fbcb1f286d2144a78efd20ed0892ecfe41ebce07390f4dc0626e842ccc7a" :answer/id #uuid "b0e5d284-f41a-5cea-8761-170e9e603d9c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-{e}^{-s}\\cdot \\frac{5\\pi }{{s}^{2}+25{\\pi }^{2}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-331039/selection/522c55b8bfbf8223bc2ba6695584369d9042fdda99134d3ee6cfcd0a8815fa97" :answer/id #uuid "b3b165cc-79cb-56bd-9ce6-028f439f5a7e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{e}^{-s}\\cdot \\frac{5\\pi }{{s}^{2}+25{\\pi }^{2}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-331039/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "e98b9e1c-0f10-5f0d-b9ba-9eff964a624c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-331039/selection/ad60fbcb1f286d2144a78efd20ed0892ecfe41ebce07390f4dc0626e842ccc7a" :answer-field/choices ["q-331039/selection/dd1a4a3c7090169e73093aecca884576b55cf87dd14dafd5a8c4b8bc93b4f414" "q-331039/selection/6fa0ebd5d3d267d83a4af36945026e0eec615ab545d18b185ff4acab4ba2aaf8" "q-331039/selection/61b0be8399d0736c70c106a293a36dfcdeec4f3603994c83f678deb760e9db2d" "q-331039/selection/ad60fbcb1f286d2144a78efd20ed0892ecfe41ebce07390f4dc0626e842ccc7a" "q-331039/selection/522c55b8bfbf8223bc2ba6695584369d9042fdda99134d3ee6cfcd0a8815fa97"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-331039" :question/id #uuid "00235b12-2ebc-5328-b8e1-a300837b18e9" :question/math-academy-id "q-331039" :question/problem "Given that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L{\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\omega t} & =\\frac{\\omega }{{s}^{2}+{\\omega }^{2}}, &  & s>0, \\\\ L{\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\omega t} & =\\frac{s}{{s}^{2}+{\\omega }^{2}}, &  & s>0,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nfind $L{u(t-1)\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5\\pi t)},$ where $u(t)$ is the unit step function." :question/worked-solution "The second shifting theorem states that if $a\\ge 0$ and $L{u(t-a)\\,g(t)}$ exists for $s>{s}_{0},$ then\n\n$$\nL{u(t-a)\\,g(t)}={e}^{-as}\\,L{g(t+a)},\\,\\text{for}\\,s>{s}_{0},\n$$\n\nwhere $u(t)$ is the unit step function.\n\nIn our case, we wish to find\n\n$$\nL{u(t-1)\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5\\pi t)}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, $a=1,$ and we have \n\n$$\nL{u(t-1)\\,g(t)}={e}^{-s}\\,L{g(t+1)},\n$$\n\nwhere $g(t)=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5\\pi t).$\n\nNotice that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}g(t+1) & =sin\\,(5\\pi (t+1)) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5\\pi t+5\\pi ) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡5\\pi t\\operatorname{cos}⁡5\\pi +\\operatorname{cos}⁡5\\pi t\\operatorname{sin}⁡5\\pi  \\\\  & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡5\\pi t\\cdot (-1)+\\operatorname{cos}⁡5\\pi t\\cdot 0 \\\\  & =-\\operatorname{sin}⁡5\\pi t.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $L{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\omega t)}=\\frac{\\omega }{{s}^{2}+{\\omega }^{2}}$ for $s>0,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L{g(t+1)} & =L{-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5\\pi t)} \\\\  & =-L{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5\\pi t)} \\\\  & =-\\frac{5\\pi }{{s}^{2}+25{\\pi }^{2}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, applying the second shifting theorem, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L{u(t-1)\\,g(t)} & ={e}^{-s}\\,L{g(t+1)} \\\\  & =-{e}^{-s}\\cdot \\frac{5\\pi }{{s}^{2}+25{\\pi }^{2}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-331039/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "57cca080-3b0b-57b9-a7f8-6b1038ebd686"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-331039"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-331042/selection/a9fffec6ee27d7bf00e644755741603f520e5ab6c2dffb71f872609d169ea842" :answer/id #uuid "24f0628b-ddd2-5b3d-92cc-f307639f9c96" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-{e}^{-4s}\\cdot \\frac{5\\pi }{{s}^{2}+25{\\pi }^{2}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-331042/selection/37e4843f49203f727d9546b7f9e45f79511f82ab1642e70511529ae84862a03e" :answer/id #uuid "e617749f-5f7c-5c92-bfba-491b13f478d7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{e}^{-4s}\\cdot \\frac{5\\pi }{{s}^{2}+25{\\pi }^{2}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-331042/selection/7460fcca79bba1821f34d23369de6a86d8d08bf680e6a6ac84a1ba311b5b035e" :answer/id #uuid "c831f156-a787-5506-95bd-8b31bd7d041b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{e}^{-4s}\\cd